  - line: 13
    type: narration
    text: "Chapter 052 begins during the same transit initiated at the end of Chapter 051 and supplies no measurable ordinary-world elapsed time."
  - line: 14
    type: narration
    text: "Null-space duration, micro-second system pauses, procedural adjudication, possibility projections, Shadow Null Ingress, and subjective endless moments do not justify calendar advancement."
  - line: 15
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_internal_temporal_condition: Lingering null-space during the same departure transit begun in Chapter 051."
  - line: 16
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_pov: Geralt-centered third person"
  - line: 17
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_location: Null-space outside Zar'Vokh's jurisdictional arrival boundary, then the Shadow Null Ingress"
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_participants: Geralt; Oreck; Kyh; coherent Luminaire"
  - line: 19
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_focus: Encounter Zar'Vokh's pre-arrival jurisdiction query and bypass the normal entry mechanism without accepting its authority."
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_boundary_evidence: Chapter 052 opens inside the still-active Chapter 051 departure transit."
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "This scene ends when the party passes through Kyh's distinct on-page Shadow Null Ingress; arrival inside Zar'Vokh creates the next location and dramatic reset."
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_continuity: The Shadow Null Ingress is not the Chapter 051 departure gate."
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "It is a distinct bypass Kyh creates only after the original transit encounters Zar'Vokh's jurisdictional boundary."
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_presentation: Transit anomaly, legal threshold, and conceptual infiltration"
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_cutscene_purpose: Establish Zar'Vokh's procedural danger before physical arrival and demonstrate that normal entry would constitute jurisdictional submission."
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_hidden/unshown_intervals: The original gate's launch-to-null-space duration is unstated; no ordinary travel interval or calendar passage is supplied."
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_contradictions: Chapter 052 attributes transit residue to Ghost Spire energy even though Chapter 051 explicitly powered the departure gate with Luminaire's reserves and Pyroclast's stabilized node."
  - line: 28
    type: narration
    text: "The provenance shift is unexplained."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "Chapter 052 later also supplies a Ghost Spire retrieval tether without explaining how that tether was established or connected to Luminaire's gate."
  - line: 30
