  - line: 118
    type: narration
    text: "```"
  - line: 119
    type: narration
    text: "The silence after a Void Jump was usually brief—a heartbeat of null-space before the new world rushed in."
  - line: 121
    type: narration
    text: "This time, the silence lingered."
  - line: 123
    type: narration
    text: "They hung in a non-place, the Ghost Spire’s energy still crackling around them like dying lightning."
  - line: 124
    type: narration
    text: "Before them, instead of a world, hung a question, etched in cold, blue data-light across the void:"
  - line: 126
    type: narration
    text: "JURISDICTION QUERY: STATE ARRIVAL AUTHORITY FOR ZAR'VOKH (SPIRE-9)."
  - line: 128
    type: narration
    text: "“It knows we’re coming,” Oreck growled, his hand on his cleaver. “We haven’t even arrived.”"
  - line: 130
    type: narration
    text: "“Worse,” Luminaire’s voice was a tense hum in Geralt’s mind. “It has pre-emptively filed a motion of inquiry."
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "To step onto Zar’Vokh is to accept its jurisdiction."
  - line: 132
    type: narration
    text: "To accept is to be bound by its verdicts.”"
  - line: 134
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stared at the pulsing glyphs."
  - line: 135
    type: narration
    text: "They weren’t a barrier."
  - line: 136
    type: narration
    text: "They were a contract, waiting for his signature in the form of a single step."
  - line: 138
    type: narration
    text: "“So we don’t arrive,” said a quiet voice."
  - line: 140
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh floated beside him, his eyes fixed on the space between the glowing legal text."
  - line: 141
    type: narration
    text: "His twilight gaze saw what they didn’t: the seams in the procedural reality. “We don’t use the door."
  - line: 142
    type: narration
    text: "We use the gap where the door forgot to meet the wall.”"
  - line: 144
    type: narration
    text: "He explained the Shadow Null Ingress."
  - line: 145
    type: narration
    text: "Not a Void Jump to a location, but a slide through a crack in the filing system."
  - line: 146
    type: narration
    text: "A path that existed in the administrative silence before the first law was written."
  - line: 148
    type: narration
    text: "“It will be… cold,” Kyh warned. “Not temperature."
  - line: 149
    type: narration
    text: "Conceptual."
  - line: 150
    type: narration
    text: "It is the absence of being acknowledged."
  - line: 151
    type: narration
    text: "Most minds fray at the edges there.”"
  - line: 153
    type: narration
    text: "“Do it,” Geralt said."
  - line: 155
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh nodded."
  - line: 156
    type: narration
    text: "He didn’t open a portal."
  - line: 157
    type: narration
    text: "He pressed his hands against the fabric of reality and parted it, not into light or darkness, but into a profound, silent grey."
  - line: 158
    type: narration
    text: "A corridor of unregistered potential."
  - line: 160
    type: narration
    text: "“Don’t think of a destination,” Kyh whispered, stepping through. “Think of… nowhere.”"
  - line: 162
    type: narration
    text: "They followed."
  - line: 164
    type: narration
    text: "The sensation was instant and visceral."
  - line: 165
    type: narration
    text: "It was the feeling of being unmade as a fact."
  - line: 166
    type: narration
    text: "The Anchor bond in Geralt’s chest didn’t fade—it strained, screaming against the erasure."
  - line: 167
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire hissed in psychic pain."
  - line: 168
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck grunted, his physicality, his sheer thereness, fighting the nullity."
  - line: 170
    type: narration
    text: "And then, they were through."
  - line: 172
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"

